 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A door for «الباب», an hourglass for the forty years (a number the Quran states). No motif on Musa, Harun or the two men; their words «فاذهب أنت وربك» are never illustrated and are glossed only as As-Sa'di's condemnation; Allah is never depicted. Al-Muyassar's first-person «طاعتي» and As-Sa'di's «نحرم» not used. STAGING v4: 23 stays ambient (battle context: the two men urge the people to enter upon the mighty people and promise victory): no people, door plate for the gate of the city (23:11-15), geometric on the Name 23:17. 24-26: Musa is a blue drop with his name. The people answer him and shake their heads (24:1, 24:4); nothing is acted on 24:10-13 (no pointing, no camera move on the Lord); they sit on 24:15 as they said, then a wide shot so Musa is in frame for his prayer. Musa speaks his prayer on 25:1 (no glow, no camera move on the Lord); his brother is not drawn (not named in the verse or the tafsirs). Allah's answer (26:1) has no speaker on screen. Hourglass for the forty years (a number the Quran states); the people stand and walk to and fro on 26:7-9 for the wandering (a this-world penalty, As-Sa'di), nobody fades or is hurt."
 },
